course: dictionary
lesson: 9668
title: Places around a city
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: A suburb is an area on the edge of a city or town where people live. Most of its buildings are houses, schools and shops, not big offices or factories. Look for these clues in the text.
explain: The suburbs means all the areas like this around a city. In «the trick spread from suburb to suburb», the context tells you the cockatoos' trick moved from one area on the edge of Sydney to the next.
explain: To check your meaning, swap it into the sentence. "The trick spread from one area of houses and shops to the next" still makes sense, so suburb is probably right.
fact: A suburb is an area where people live on the edge of a city or town.
fact: The suburbs means all the suburbs around a city.
fact: Suburbs are mostly houses, schools and shops, rather than big offices or factories.
fact: Suburbs grew when trains and cars let people live further from work.
fact: In Australia and New Zealand, people often name their suburb: Bondi is a suburb of Sydney.
exercise: «Cockatoos learned to flip open wheelie bins and the trick spread from suburb to suburb.» What is a suburb here? | A kind of wheelie bin | A big factory with offices | *An area on the edge of a city, with houses and shops | A bird that sings
exercise: Where would you most likely find the suburbs? | *Around the edge of a city, with houses, schools and shops | Only in the countryside, far from any town | In the middle of the sea | Inside a big factory
exercise: Which place is a suburb? | The middle of the Pacific Ocean | A village with only one farm | *Bondi, an area of Sydney with houses and shops | Sahara Desert, a sea of sand with no homes
test: «In the film, the suburbs were quiet streets with gardens and driveways.» What are the suburbs like in this film? | *Quiet streets with gardens and driveways | Under the sea | Loud and busy with tall towers | Covered in snow all year
test: Why did suburbs grow? | Because factories were built on every street | Because cities were banned | Because people wanted to live in deserts | *Because trains and cars let people live further from work
exam: Which sentence describes a suburb best? | A busy sea port with ships | *A street of houses and shops on the edge of a city | A huge office tower in the centre of a city | A field full of sheep in the middle of the countryside
